-- title:
--   Reducedness of the Taylor–Wiles level Hecke ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative local integral domain of characteristic zero, with residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$. Let $N,r\ge 1$ be natural numbers and let $qv\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,t\to\mathbb N$ be a tuple of nonzero natural numbers, so that the auxiliary level is $\mathrm{level}\,N\,r\,qv=N\cdot\bigl(\prod_i qv_i\bigr)\cdot r$. Let $S$ be a set of natural numbers and $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/\mathrm{level}\,N\,r\,qv)^\times$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(N))\bigr)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$ — to $k$, and let $\alpha\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,t\to k$ be a tuple of residue-field elements. Assume two commutativity hypotheses: `OpComm`, that the operators $\mathrm{op}\,g$ attached to all $g:\mathrm{Gen}\,(\mathrm{level}\,N\,r\,qv)\,S\,t$ commute with one another, and `DiaComm`, that each diamond operator $\mathrm{diamondL}\,u$, $u\in(\mathbb Z/\mathrm{level}\,N\,r\,qv)^\times$, commutes with every $\mathrm{op}\,g$. The conclusion is that the ring `HeckeRing N r qv S 𝒪 H θ α hc hdc`, namely the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(\mathrm{ML}\,N\,r\,qv\,S\,\mathcal O\,H\,\theta\,\alpha\,hc)$ generated by the set `heckeRingGens N r qv S 𝒪 H θ α hc hdc`, is reduced: it has no nonzero nilpotent element.
--
--   This records the reducedness of the Hecke ring acting on the localised cohomology module at a Taylor–Wiles auxiliary level, obtained from the semisimplicity of commuting Hecke operators in characteristic zero. It is invoked in the construction of the associated Galois representation and in the structural results on the Hecke ring used in the patching argument, for instance in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_galoisRepAdic_trace_frobenius_eq_T`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_galoisRepAdic_trace_frobenius_eq_T) and [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_basis_inertia_apply_eq_diamond_smul`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_basis_inertia_apply_eq_diamond_smul).
